{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:ffc15457247e:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/codex_review.py:255", "observed_evidence": "Concurrency flaw in failover row counting. The `before` and `after` checks count all `GEMINI_PRODUCER` rows globally in the shared `merge-gate-log.jsonl` rather than filtering by the current `arc_id` and `round_n`. A concurrent review on another lane emitting a gemini row will artificially increment `after`, causing this run to falsely conclude its failover subprocess already emitted the row and incorrectly drop its own `REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE` record.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:238ea548e92d:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:523", "observed_evidence": "`run_with_retry` ignores `att.returncode` entirely. If a reviewer process crashes with a non-zero exit code but happens to emit a valid JSON block before terminating, this loop incorrectly accepts the verdict instead of returning `REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE`. This violates the contract asserted in `test_review_preserves_findings_on_nonzero_agy_exit`.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:519788faf2e4:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/codex_review.py:115", "observed_evidence": "Unsafe state handling via strict float comparison. `started_at <= mtime <= now` compares fractional `time.time()` against filesystem `mtime` which may suffer from truncation or granularity issues (e.g., ext4 truncating fractional seconds). An artifact written immediately after `started_wall` could receive a truncated `mtime` strictly smaller than the `started_at` float, permanently excluding it and causing an artificial timeout.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:30d80ff6f110:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/codex_review.py:257", "observed_evidence": "Uncaught `FileNotFoundError` in `_run_gemini_failover`. If `just` is missing from `PATH` (e.g., if the wrapper is invoked directly via `uv run python` instead of through `just`), `subprocess.run` raises `FileNotFoundError`. This crashes the script completely rather than gracefully yielding a permanent `REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE` as mandated by the `C-HE-16` classification table.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:c6b287224fa0:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:441", "observed_evidence": "`compute_binding` calls `subprocess.run` with `text=True` for the `git diff` payload, and later `.encode()`s it to compute the SHA-256 digest. If the repository diff contains non-UTF-8 byte sequences, this throws a `UnicodeDecodeError` and fatally crashes the wrapper. (It should capture raw bytes).", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
